      '@type': 'Answer',
      text: 'Pass timeout_ms to ExactModelBrowserHost.execute on npm traverse-embedder-web@0.17.1, or put timeout_ms on the model.execute payload for ExactModelHostConnector in crates.io traverse-runtime 0.17.1. The host uses the smaller of timeout_ms and the package manifest max_execution_ms. On a browser Worker and on wasmtime, a deadline that lands during the call stops the guest and the call fails with timeout. On Node, and with createWorker: null, the host checks the deadline before the call and again after the guest returns. A guest that never returns stays running on that path. Registration can also take a per-placement preparation budget. Aborting that signal fails with cancelled and keeps nothing.',
